{"id":"cd35e336-e9d1-4eda-b458-d10fe6d2c061","object":"chat.completion","created":1793240176,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I now have complete evidence for the mechanisms (EnvVar descriptor + factory methods, rearm/rearm_all, NewLineFormatter, _setup_logger, init_logger, and stats_logger's `_log_worker`/`_emit_logs`). Let me write a note grounding each mechanism before editing.\n\n```python\nn1 = write_note(\n    title=\"config-logger-stats mechanisms\",\n    content=(\n        \"environ.py: EnvVar descriptor caches on first access via owner.__dict__.get; init exceptions wrapped with 'Name: msg' by raising type(e)(f\\\"{self.name}: {e}\\\"). Factory methods int/float/bool/str/str_or_none/int_or_none/choice define init lambdas. _int uses int(v) if v is not None else default. Repo ends with global envs object; rearm(name) resets one descriptor, rearm_all() resets all, so cached values persist until rear* is called. \"\n        \"logger.py: NewLineFormatter(fmt, datefmt, high_precision, use_color) overrides formatTime and format; format calls super().format(record), then aligns multiline via record.message prefix and optional color. _setup_logger creates a single StreamHandler (only if _default_handler is None) and then always setFormatter(NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=isatty)). init_logger sets level DEBUG and reuses root handler via propagate for deepinfer.* names, else adds _default_handler if missing. \"\n        \"stats_logger.py: `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger`; module logger = init_logger(__name__). _emit_logs puts list[str] on queue; _log_worker iterates q.get until None, sleeps by rank%8, calls `logger.info(m)` per message. That is the consumer where extra={'keep_full_message': True} belongs.\"\n    ),\n    evidence_ids=[\n        \"ev-3b2d7658cb0fabb40a3d\",\"ev-246c6e73a88cb2c9edc3\",\"ev-8554ade850ecb397d235\",\"ev-ef45633e339c9e5fd82f\",\"ev-ed2914917db6a069f2c